{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Built and locally validated a three-case actor-layer probe (draft/omnipaxos_runtime/tests/assurance_generated.rs) and filed it as the fixed experiment, switching the crate basis to `omnipaxos_runtime` because the run's configured `omnipaxos` harness target cannot link the actor layer. The probe runs one real 3-node in-process cluster shape: mode A (control, no partition) resolves `Ok` with the caller's entry at the returned index; modes B and C cut the forced leader from both followers, let it accept the entry only locally, let node 3 decide a different entry at the same index, then reconnect the origin. Native local feedback (not retained evidence) reproduced the two arms the source reasoning predicts: `Superseded` with 2 ms ticks (3/3) versus `Ok(assigned_idx)` with 80 ms ticks (5/5) while the decided entry at that index was the new leader's entry — so the registered hypothesis was narrowed to the tick race between the origin's promise change and its decided-index advance, and the investigation's hypothesis/discriminator were updated accordingly. Two source anchors for the tick quantisation were added. Incomplete: the formal receipt for the submitted experiment is pending, and the question-level Interpretation still carries `unresolved`/`unresolved` until that receipt is interpreted.\"}"}}
